{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.NonCrossingPartitions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.NonCrossingPartitions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Central","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_eq_catalan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_eq_catalan","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L176-L193","doc":"**The count is the Catalan number.** `|NC(n)| = Fintype.card (NCPart n)\n= Nat.centralBinom n / (n+1) = C_n` for `n = 0,1,2,3,4`. This is the\nbijective upgrade of `FreeCumulants.freeMoment_eval_one_eq_catalanCount`:\nthere the all-ones moment *evaluated* to `C_n`; here the non-crossing\npartitions are *counted* and the count *is* `C_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.catalan_via_centralBinom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.catalan_via_centralBinom","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L168-L174","doc":"The Catalan values `C₀..C₄ = 1,1,2,5,14`, via Mathlib's\n`Nat.centralBinom` (`C_n = centralBinom n / (n+1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.crossingLabel_not_nonCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.crossingLabel_not_nonCrossing","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L158-L161","doc":"…but it **crosses** (`i,j,k,l = 0,1,2,3` with `f 0 = f 2`, `f 1 = f 3`,\n`f 0 ≠ f 1`), so it is excluded from `NCPart 4`. This lone exclusion is\n`15 − 14 = 1`, the freeness signature of `FreeCumulants.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.crossingLabel_isCanon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.crossingLabel_isCanon","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L155-L156","doc":"`crossingLabel` **is** a valid canonical partition labelling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.crossingLabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.crossingLabel","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L151-L153","doc":"The crossing partition's canonical block-label function\n`f = (0,1,0,1)` on `Fin 4` (blocks `{0,2}` and `{1,3}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_four","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L139-L141","doc":"`|NC(4)| = 14 = C₄`.  The 15th partition of `{0,1,2,3}` — the crossing\n`{{0,2},{1,3}}` — is the one `NonCross` rejects (see below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_three","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L136-L137","doc":"`|NC(3)| = 5 = C₃`  (all 5 partitions of a 3-set are non-crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_two","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L133-L134","doc":"`|NC(2)| = 2 = C₂`  (`{{0},{1}}`, `{{0,1}}` — both non-crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_one","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L130-L131","doc":"`|NC(1)| = 1 = C₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.card_ncpart_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L127-L128","doc":"`|NC(0)| = 1 = C₀` (the empty partition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instDecidableEqNCPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instDecidableEqNCPart","kind":"instance","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L118-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instFintypeNCPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instFintypeNCPart","kind":"instance","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L115-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instDecidablePredNCPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instDecidablePredNCPart","kind":"instance","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L111-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instDecidableNonCross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instDecidableNonCross","kind":"instance","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L108-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.instDecidableIsCanon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.instDecidableIsCanon","kind":"instance","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L105-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NCPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NCPart","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L100-L103","doc":"The **non-crossing partitions of `Fin n`**, encoded as canonical\nblock-label functions with no crossing. A `Fintype` with `DecidableEq`\n(derived below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.NonCross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.NonCross","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L94-L98","doc":"`f` is **non-crossing**: no `i < j < k < l` has `f i = f k`,\n`f j = f l`, `f i ≠ f j` (two blocks interleaving as `…i…j…k…l…`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IsCanon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IsCanon","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/NonCrossingPartitions.lean#L86-L92","doc":"`f : Fin n → Fin n` is a **canonical partition labelling**: `f i` is\nthe minimum of the block containing `i`. Characterised by `f i ≤ i`\n(representative is the block minimum) and `f (f i) = f i` (representatives\nare fixed points). These two conditions cut the finite function type\n`Fin n → Fin n` down to the partition lattice of `Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}